    {
      "id": "1559267339713642547",
      "type": "Default",
      "timestamp": "2026-10-12T18:11:43.574+00:00",
      "timestampEdited": null,
      "callEndedTimestamp": null,
      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "@Paul if you are interested and @Tholin is willing, I would be happy to help out integrating a SoC with Tholin's voltage regulator for one of the slots if that would be of interest.  I wouldn't be able to do a self trimming oscillator as Tim suggested (though if anyone else here is available to do that I'd be happy to integrate it), but we could have something that was either driven from a ring oscillator or an external clock, with the ability to do USB CDC (traditional Full Speed only) if an external clock is supplied.  We'd use the latest version of Tholin's standard cell library to prove that works as expected in a complex project.  I haven't looked into Staf's SRAMs, but potentially we could use them as well, providing initial results from run 2 are positive.\n\nI've recently been working on an improved version of BIO - with more predictable instruction timing and improved instruction set over Baochip's BIO (https://www.crowdsupply.com/baochip/dabao/updates/bio-the-bao-i-o-co-processor), I don't know how usable that will be by the run 3 deadline but it would be cool to have the opportunity to tape it out even if it was a bit WIP.",
      "author": {
        "id": "691780627338625077",
        "name": "rebelmike",
        "discriminator": "0000",
        "nickname": "RebelMike",
        "color": null,
        "isBot": false,
        "roles": [],
        "avatarUrl": "2026-10_media/49aaff687e56f04e7bbdedf0077bab75-7DDB4.png"
